Translation patch: `value::convert::chrono`: chrono calls go through `trusted`

Change: `NaiveDate::from_ymd_opt`, `NaiveTime::from_hms_micro_opt`, `NaiveDateTime::new` and the `Datelike`/`Timelike` getters become the corresponding `trusted::naive_*` helpers. For a `NaiveDateTime x`, `x.year()`/`month()`/`day()` become the `NaiveDate` getters of `x.date()` and `x.hour()`/`minute()`/`second()`/`nanosecond()` the `NaiveTime` getters of `x.time()` (both computed once, before the year check).
Why: chrono is not translated (see patch 40).
Behaviour: Identical: chrono 0.4.45 implements `Datelike`/`Timelike` for `NaiveDateTime` by delegating to its `date`/`time` fields, which `date()`/`time()` return; the getters are pure.

